 "notes": [
  "Produced by tests/interop/compare.sh with the repository Go harness: three rounds, server order alternating each round, one sample per workload per round.",
  "The upstream v1.15.2 Go client drives both servers. Medians include every sample, including invalid ones.",
  "Paced workloads send one reliable ordered request per interval per connection; saturated workloads keep one request outstanding with no pacing and are overload characterization.",
  "Impaired workloads run inside a disposable network namespace with netem on loopback; RTT is the added round trip.",
  "RTT is localhost echo time measured by the client, not player ping. It uses each connection's last 2048 samples and includes drained replies; throughput excludes the drain.",
  "RSS is the larger measurement endpoint, not peak RSS. CPU 100% is one logical CPU."
 ],
